\item \strong{\code{return_value = "both"} (recommended)} — the helper returns a list
with both \verb{$result} and \verb{$conditions}, and you re-assign externally:

\preformatted{
   out <- cacs_capture_conditions(
     cacs_acs_prefetch(state = "AL", year = 2023),
     return_value = "both"
   )
   acs <- out$result
   nrow(out$conditions)  # how many water-tract messages were emitted
   }
\item \strong{\verb{<<-} super-assignment} — \verb{<<-} walks the search path so the binding
lands in the global environment (or the script's calling environment):

